@startuml A2-analysis-activity-diagram
title UC-ADM-02 – Activity diagram (main flow + A1-A4)
start
note right
  The System administrator role always includes the permission to
  manage roles and permissions. A1 therefore applies to any other
  requester, or to an account whose role does not grant it.
end note
:1. Administrator locates a user account;
if (Requester holds the permission to\nmanage roles and permissions\n(granted through its role)?) then (no)
  :A1. Reject request;
  :Assignment unchanged;
  stop
else (yes)
endif
:2. System shows current role assignments\nand account status;
:3. Administrator selects or changes a role assignment;
:4. System validates the change against available\nroles and access-control rules\n(the user must keep at least one role);
if (Valid?) then (no)
  :A2. Explain the issue;
  :Assignment unchanged;
  stop
else (yes)
endif
if (Own privileges or\ndesignated sensitive assignment?) then (yes)
  :A4. Apply the applicable safeguards;
else (no)
endif
:5. Administrator reviews and confirms the change;
if (Saved?) then (no)
  :A3. Report the failure;
  :Do not claim access changed;
  :Assignment unchanged;
  stop
else (yes)
endif
:6. System saves the assignment and\nconfirms the effective result;
:Change is attributable and available for audit;
stop
@enduml
